<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Patient Monitor — Mist Examples</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/mistexamples.css?v=4">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/patientmonitor.css?v=4">
</head>
<body>
    <header class="site-header">
        <div class="site-header__inner">
            <a href="/MistExamples" class="brand">
                <span class="mist-mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                <span>Mist</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/MistExamples" class="site-header__link">All examples</a>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="container detail-page detail-page--wide">
        <header class="example-intro">
            <span class="badge">InstanceComponent</span>
            <h1>Patient monitor</h1>
            <p>See stable clinical records and changing bedside telemetry joined in one live interface.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="demo-stage demo-stage--monitor">
            <div class="demo-stage__bar">
                <span class="live-status">Live example</span>
                <code>PatientComponent</code>
            </div>
            <div class="demo-stage__body">
                <section class="patient-grid">
                    #for(context in contexts):
                        #extend("PatientMonitorExample/PatientComponent")
                    #endfor
                </section>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="implementation-note">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
                <h2>Two sources, one component</h2>
            </div>
            <p>
                Each <code>InstanceComponent</code> joins an EMR patient row with a live vitals row through their shared UUID. A database change redraws only that patient's card, keeping the identity and telemetry in sync.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
    
    <script src="/morphdom.js"></script>
    <script src="/mist.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
